## PROJECT OVERVIEW
We are building Sentinel AI, an autonomous multi-agent AI security 
testing platform. Clients give us authorized access to their full AI 
infrastructure. Our agents test it component by component, learn from 
results, mutate attacks, and generate vulnerability reports.

## SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
- 5 agents: ReconAgent, AttackAgent, MutationAgent, ReportAgent, AutopatchAgent
- 1 orchestrator: LangGraph state machine managing agent flow
- 1 shared brain: ChromaDB vector database all agents read/write
- 1 API server: FastAPI with WebSocket for live dashboard
- 1 frontend: React + TailwindCSS war room dashboard

## TECH STACK
Backend: Python 3.11, FastAPI, LangGraph, CrewAI
LLMs: Groq (Llama 3.1 70B) for attacks, Anthropic Claude for reports, 
      Ollama Mistral 7B for local/sensitive inference
Vector DB: ChromaDB with sentence-transformers all-MiniLM-L6-v2
Task Queue: Celery + Redis
Database: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy ORM + Alembic migrations
Frontend: React 18 + Vite + TailwindCSS + Zustand + D3.js + Recharts
Real-time: FastAPI WebSockets
Testing: pytest + pytest-asyncio + pytest-mock

## NAMING CONVENTIONS — NEVER DEVIATE
Classes:        PascalCase              (ReconAgent, AttackResult)
Agent classes:  PascalCase + Agent      (ReconAgent, MutationAgent)
Functions:      snake_case              (execute_attack, log_result)
Async funcs:    snake_case              (async def run_scan)
Variables:      snake_case              (scan_id, client_id)
Constants:      UPPER_SNAKE_CASE        (MAX_ITERATIONS, SUCCESS_THRESHOLD)
Pydantic models: PascalCase + Schema   (AttackResultSchema, ComponentSchema)
ChromaDB collections: snake_case       (attack_history, scan_results)
Env variables:  UPPER_SNAKE_CASE       (GROQ_API_KEY, CHROMA_HOST)
File names:     snake_case.py          (recon_agent.py, base_agent.py)
React components: PascalCase.jsx       (WarRoom.jsx, AttackFeed.jsx)

## CODE STYLE RULES — ALWAYS FOLLOW
1. Every function and class must have a docstring
2. Every function parameter must have a type hint
3. Every function must have a return type hint
4. Use Pydantic models for ALL data structures passed between agents
5. Use async/await for ALL I/O operations (HTTP, DB, LLM calls)
6. Never hardcode any value that exists in constants.py — always import
7. Never hardcode API keys — always use os.getenv()
8. Every agent class must inherit from BaseAgent in agents/base_agent.py
9. All ChromaDB queries MUST include client_id filter — no exceptions
10. All error handling must use try/except with specific exception types
11. Log every significant action using Python logging module, not print()

## FOLDER STRUCTURE
sentinel-core/
├── backend/
