│       ├── components/      # React components
│       ├── store/           # Zustand state
│       └── hooks/           # Custom React hooks
├── tests/
├── constants.py             # ALL shared constants live here
├── .env.example
├── .cursorrules             # This file
├── docker-compose.yml
└── requirements.txt

## IMPORTS ORDER (follow this exactly)
1. Standard library imports
2. Third party imports
3. Local imports (from agents.base_agent import BaseAgent)

## AGENT COMMUNICATION PATTERN
All agents communicate ONLY through:
1. The LangGraph state object (for workflow state)
2. ChromaDB (for knowledge and results)
Never pass data between agents directly as function arguments.

## SECURITY RULES (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
1. Every scan requires a valid consent_id in the database before starting
2. All ChromaDB queries filter by client_id
3. No attack executes without the scan being in ACTIVE status in PostgreSQL
4. Autopatch agent checks approved_findings list before every patch action
5. All client credentials are stored encrypted, never in plain text
